// title: Wyoming Primary Election Participation Survey
{
  "title": "Wyoming Primary Election Participation Survey",
  "description": "Measure Wyoming voter perspectives on primary participation, party nomination rights, privacy, election administration, and public reporting.",
  "x_meta": {
    "flow": "sectioned",
    "sectionExitEnabled": true,
    "sectionExitLabel": "End of section",
    "exitUrl": "/surveys/list/",
    "path": "divisive",
    "category_slug": "primary-elections",
    "estimated_minutes": 7,
    "featured": true
  },
  "showQuestionNumbers": "off",
  "questionTitleLocation": "top",
  "checkErrorsMode": "onValueChanged",
  "completeText": "Submit survey",
  "completedHtml": "<h3>Thank you.</h3><p>Your response has been recorded.</p>",
  "pages": [
    {
      "name": "overview",
      "elements": [
        {
          "type": "html",
          "name": "survey_overview",
          "html": "<h3>Purpose</h3><p>This survey asks Wyoming voters how primary elections should work. The goal is to measure public opinion on voter participation, party nomination rights, privacy, election administration, and public reporting.</p><h3>How responses will be used</h3><p>This survey is a tool to gather and report registered Wyoming voter survey results in aggregate. Exact question wording, response options, collection dates, sample size, verification method, and revision notes will be published with the results. Individual responses will remain confidential.</p><h3>Verification note</h3><p>For Wyoming voters, responses may be verified against a voter-file data set obtained from the Wyoming Secretary of State. The current verification file reflects registered voter records as of August 2025.</p><p>This serves two purposes:</p><ul><li>It helps report survey results from verified registered Wyoming voters.</li><li>It can help a respondent see whether the submitted information matches a registered voter record in the August 2025 file.</li></ul><p>A match confirms the respondent appeared in that data file. It does not confirm later registration changes, current party affiliation, or current voter status after August 2025. If a respondent registered, moved, or updated voter information after August 2025, the match result may need additional review.</p><p>Where possible, county, State House district, and State Senate district will come from the voter-file match instead of asking extra questions. Verified and unverified results should be reported separately.</p><h3>Background note</h3><p>Wyoming currently uses a closed primary system for major party nomination contests. Registered voters must declare or change party affiliation before receiving a major party primary ballot. In 2026, the party-affiliation change deadline was May 13, and candidate filing opened May 14.</p><h3>References used to draft this survey</h3><p>These links are provided for voters who want to review the source material. Reading them is optional and is not required to answer the survey. The questions below are intended to measure opinion, not persuade.</p><ul><li><a href=\"https://wyoleg.gov/statutes/compress/title97.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Wyoming Constitution, Article 1</a></li><li><a href=\"https://law.justia.com/codes/wyoming/title-22/chapter-5/article-2/section-22-5-212/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Wyoming Election Code, W.S. 22-5-212</a></li><li><a href=\"https://law.justia.com/codes/wyoming/title-22/chapter-5/article-2/section-22-5-214/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Wyoming Election Code, W.S. 22-5-214</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.campbellcountywy.gov/867/Elections\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">2026 Wyoming election calendar example, Campbell County</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.law.cornell.edu/supremecourt/text/99-401\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">California Democratic Party v. Jones</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.law.cornell.edu/supremecourt/text/479/208\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Tashjian v. Republican Party of Connecticut</a></li></ul>"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "current_understanding",
      "title": "Section 1: Current understanding",
      "elements": [
        {
          "type": "radiogroup",
          "name": "familiarity_with_current_rules",
          "title": "1. How familiar are you with Wyoming's current primary election rules?",
          "isRequired": true,
          "choices": [
            "Very familiar",
            "Somewhat familiar",
            "Slightly familiar",
            "Unfamiliar",
            "Not sure"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "radiogroup",
          "name": "knew_party_affiliation_requirement",
          "title": "2. Before this survey, did you know registered voters must declare or change party affiliation before receiving a major party primary ballot?",
          "isRequired": true,
          "choices": [
            "Yes",
            "No",
            "Not sure"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "radiogroup",
          "name": "knew_deadline_before_candidate_filing",
          "title": "3. Before this survey, did you know the 2026 party-affiliation deadline came before the candidate filing period opened?",
          "isRequired": true,
          "choices": [
            "Yes",
            "No",
            "Not sure"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "preferred_primary_structure",
      "title": "Section 2: Preferred primary structure",
      "elements": [
        {
          "type": "radiogroup",
          "name": "preferred_primary_system",
          "title": "4. Which primary election system do you prefer for Wyoming?",
          "isRequired": true,
          "choices": [
            "Current closed primary system",
            "Major party primaries open to unaffiliated voters only",
            "Major party primaries open to any registered voter, with each voter choosing one party ballot",
            "One primary ballot with all candidates, with the top two advancing",
            "One primary ballot with all candidates, with the top four advancing",
            "Another system",
            "Not sure"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "radiogroup",
          "name": "eligibility_for_party_ballot",
          "title": "5. If Wyoming keeps party primaries, who should be eligible to choose a major party primary ballot?",
          "isRequired": true,
          "choices": [
            "Only voters already affiliated with that party",
            "Voters affiliated with that party plus unaffiliated voters",
            "Any registered voter, limited to one party ballot per election",
            "Each party should decide who may participate",
            "Not sure"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "radiogroup",
          "name": "ballot_choice_changes_affiliation",
          "title": "6. Should choosing a party primary ballot automatically change a voter's official party affiliation?",
          "isRequired": true,
          "choices": [
            "Yes",
            "No",
            "Only if the voter requests the change",
            "Not sure"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "balancing_principles",
      "title": "Section 3: Balancing principles",
      "elements": [
        {
          "type": "radiogroup",
          "name": "most_important_principle",
          "title": "7. Which principle should receive the most weight in Wyoming primary election law?",
          "isRequired": true,
          "choices": [
            "Voter access to publicly funded primary elections",
            "Party association in choosing nominees",
            "Election administration and clear rules",
            "Voter privacy in ballot choice",
            "Equal treatment of registered voters",
            "Not sure"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "radiogroup",
          "name": "fairness_when_principles_conflict",
          "title": "8. When voter access and party nomination rights conflict, which approach feels most fair?",
          "isRequired": true,
          "choices": [
            "Give more weight to voter access",
            "Give more weight to party nomination rights",
            "Balance both as evenly as possible",
            "Depends on the office or election",
            "Not sure"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "radiogroup",
          "name": "allow_party_choice_for_unaffiliated",
          "title": "9. Should state law allow each major party to decide whether unaffiliated voters may participate in that party's primary?",
          "isRequired": true,
          "choices": [
            "Yes",
            "No",
            "Only if the rule is published before candidate filing begins",
            "Not sure"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "deadline_timing",
      "title": "Section 4: Deadline timing",
      "elements": [
        {
          "type": "radiogroup",
          "name": "preferred_affiliation_deadline_timing",
          "title": "10. Should party-affiliation deadlines be set before or after the candidate filing period?",
          "isRequired": true,
          "choices": [
            "Before candidate filing opens",
            "After candidate filing closes",
            "Same day candidate filing closes",
            "Keep the current timeline",
            "Not sure"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "radiogroup",
          "name": "importance_of_candidate_list_before_deadline",
          "title": "11. How important is it for voters to know the full candidate list before a party-affiliation deadline?",
          "isRequired": true,
          "choices": [
            "Very important",
            "Important",
            "Somewhat important",
            "Not important",
            "Not sure"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "benefits_and_concerns",
      "title": "Section 5: Benefits and concerns",
      "elements": [
        {
          "type": "checkbox",
          "name": "benefits_of_more_open_primary",
          "title": "12. What possible benefits of a more open primary system matter most to you? Pick up to 3.",
          "isRequired": true,
          "maxSelectedChoices": 3,
          "choices": [
            "More registered voters can participate in primary contests",
            "Unaffiliated voters have more ballot choice",
            "Voters have more privacy in political participation",
            "Candidates may speak to a broader voter base",
            "Primary results may better reflect the broader electorate",
            "Less influence by party leadership in nomination contests",
            "Not sure"
          ],
          "showOtherItem": true,
          "otherText": "Other"
        },
        {
          "type": "checkbox",
          "name": "concerns_about_more_open_primary",
          "title": "13. What possible concerns about a more open primary system matter most to you? Pick up to 3.",
          "isRequired": true,
          "maxSelectedChoices": 3,
          "choices": [
            "Voters outside a party may influence that party's nominee",
            "Strategic voting across party lines",
            "Weaker party identity or party accountability",
            "More complex election administration",
            "More voter confusion",
            "Higher chance of litigation",
            "Not sure"
          ],
          "showOtherItem": true,
          "otherText": "Other"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "public_reporting_and_accountability",
      "title": "Section 6: Public reporting and accountability",
      "elements": [
        {
          "type": "radiogroup",
          "name": "publish_participation_reports",
          "title": "14. Should Wyoming publish public reports showing primary participation rates by registration category and ballot type?",
          "isRequired": true,
          "choices": [
            "Yes",
            "No",
            "Only statewide",
            "By county and legislative district",
            "Not sure"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "checkbox",
          "name": "reporting_fields_preference",
          "title": "15. What information should be published with primary election reports? Pick up to 3.",
          "isRequired": true,
          "maxSelectedChoices": 3,
          "choices": [
            "Total turnout",
            "Turnout by party affiliation or registration category",
            "Number of unaffiliated voters",
            "Number of voters receiving limited ballots",
            "Number of voters changing affiliation before the deadline",
            "Number of new voters registering after the deadline",
            "County and district-level summaries",
            "Not sure"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "open_response",
      "title": "Section 7: Open response",
      "elements": [
        {
          "type": "comment",
          "name": "best_primary_system_open_response",
          "title": "16. In your own words, what primary election system would best serve Wyoming voters?",
          "isRequired": false,
          "maxLength": 1200,
          "placeholder": "Long answer, optional."
        },
        {
          "type": "comment",
          "name": "lawmakers_consideration_open_response",
